       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg is double the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You could titrate up to 10 mg.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If you really intend this, for example as a specialist-directed plan, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that the dose is intentional.\n\nIf 20 mg was meant to be 2.5 mg or 10 mg, or if you wanted a different agent added for more blood pressure control, I can enter that instead."
